        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Mini PCs have long since become more than just simple office computers. They sit on your desk, behind your monitor, in the living room or in your home lab, where they handle tasks that used to require a large desktop PC. That\u2019s precisely why it\u2019s worth taking a look inside: If you properly assess the RAM, SSD, Wi-Fi, and ports before buying, you can upgrade a compact system later on as needed, rather than replacing it prematurely.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>However, there is less scope for customization than with traditional tower PCs. Compact cases, soldered components, and confined cooling systems set clear limits. Nevertheless, RAM, an SSD, a Wi-Fi module or an external graphics solution can make all the difference \u2014 between a mini PC that\u2019s barely adequate and a system that will remain useful for several more years.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"what-can-actua",
